              "id": "tab_1",
              "kind": "history_physical",
              "title": "History and Physical",
              "blocks": [
                {
                  "kind": "markdown",
                  "value": "Chief concern: The client is brought to the emergency department by a roommate after 2 days of nausea, vomiting and abdominal pain. The roommate says the client has been drinking water all day, urinating often and breathing fast since last night."
                },
                {
                  "kind": "markdown",
                  "value": "History: Type 1 diabetes mellitus diagnosed at age 11. Uses an insulin pump. The pump's infusion set came out 2 days ago during a hiking trip and was not replaced, because the client felt too sick to eat. No other medical conditions. No surgeries. No known allergies. Does not smoke or drink alcohol."
                },
                {
                  "kind": "markdown",
                  "value": "Medications at home: Insulin lispro by pump, with a basal rate of 0.8 units/h and a bolus with each meal. Carries glucose tablets. Takes no other medicines or supplements."
                },
                {
                  "kind": "markdown",
                  "value": "Physical examination: Drowsy, but answers questions when spoken to. Lips and tongue are dry, and the skin on the forearm stays tented when pinched. Breathing is deep and fast, and the breath smells fruity. Lungs are clear. Heart rate is fast and regular. Abdomen is soft and tender all over, with no guarding. Capillary refill is 4 seconds."
                }
              ]
            },
            {
              "id": "tab_2",
              "kind": "nurses_notes",
              "title": "Nurses' Notes",
              "blocks": [
                {
                  "kind": "markdown",
                  "value": "Day 1, 0900: Client arrives by private car with a roommate. Drowsy, oriented to person and place. Reports nausea, thirst and abdominal pain rated 6 on a scale of 0 to 10. Fingerstick glucose reads HI. Placed on the cardiac monitor. Two large-bore IV catheters started."
                },
                {
                  "kind": "markdown",
                  "value": "Day 1, 0930: Laboratory samples sent. Urine dipstick shows large ketones and large glucose. Client vomited 150 mL of green fluid. Respirations are deep and fast.",
                  "fromStep": 2
                },
                {
                  "kind": "markdown",
                  "value": "Day 1, 0945: Provider at the bedside. Prescriptions received and read back.",
                  "fromStep": 3
                },
                {
                  "kind": "markdown",
                  "value": "Day 1, 1000: First liter of 0.9% sodium chloride started as a bolus through the IV in the left forearm. Client asks for water to drink.",
                  "fromStep": 4
                },
                {
                  "kind": "markdown",
                  "value": "Day 1, 1100: First liter of 0.9% sodium chloride finished. Regular insulin infusion started at 0.1 units/kg/h after the potassium result was reviewed with the provider. Potassium chloride added to the IV fluid as prescribed.",
                  "fromStep": 5
                },
                {
                  "kind": "markdown",
                  "value": "Day 1, 1200: Client is more alert and is oriented to person, place and time. Urine output 60 mL in the last hour. No vomiting since 0930.",
                  "fromStep": 5
                },
                {
                  "kind": "markdown",
                  "value": "Day 1, 1400: Client is awake and talking with the roommate. Reports hunger and no nausea. Breathing is quiet and regular.",
                  "fromStep": 6
                },
                {
                  "kind": "markdown",
                  "value": "Day 1, 1500: Diabetes educator paged at the client's request to review insulin pump site changes and sick-day rules.",
                  "fromStep": 6
                }
              ]
            },
