                {
                  "kind": "markdown",
                  "value": "0945: 0.9% sodium chloride 1,000 mL IV over 1 hour, then 500 mL/h.",
                  "fromStep": 3
                },
                {
                  "kind": "markdown",
                  "value": "0945: Regular insulin IV infusion at 0.1 units/kg/h, to start after the potassium result is reviewed.",
                  "fromStep": 3
                },
                {
                  "kind": "markdown",
                  "value": "0945: Fingerstick glucose every hour. Serum potassium every 2 hours.",
                  "fromStep": 3
                },
                {
                  "kind": "markdown",
                  "value": "0945: Nothing by mouth except ice chips. Strict intake and output.",
                  "fromStep": 3
                },
                {
                  "kind": "markdown",
                  "value": "1100: Add potassium chloride 20 mEq to each liter of IV fluid.",
                  "fromStep": 5
                },
                {
                  "kind": "markdown",
                  "value": "1400: Change the IV fluid to 5% dextrose in 0.45% sodium chloride when the glucose is below 250 mg/dL.",
                  "fromStep": 6
                },
                {
                  "kind": "markdown",
                  "value": "1400: Give subcutaneous insulin 2 hours before the insulin infusion is stopped.",
                  "fromStep": 6
                }
              ]
            }
